    "body": "**Hands-on check passed** on a fresh macOS build of this branch, run by the contributor (screenshots in hand).\n\n- **Light theme:** every browser row's text is dark and readable, and so is the selected row on its highlight. The trailing text and hidden rows are a softer grey but still clear.\n- **Icons and the eye:** the first round showed the row icons and the eye washed out on Light, because they were tinted plain white. Fixed in 1fc5104d: each row's icon takes the row's text ink and its eye the trailing-text ink. Re-checked: the icons, the eye and the eye-off icon are all clearly visible on Light.\n- **Dark theme:** rows, icons and eyes all read well.\n- **The OS appearance no longer moves the theme:** with CamCraft open, switching macOS between Light and Dark left CamCraft on the theme picked in Theme….\n\nSince 1fc5104d, `tree_ink_tests` passes 2/2 and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean. Marking ready for review.\n",
